<id/doc/doc_star_anise/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Star Anise"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_spices_condiments/#concept> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1760637> ;
    skos:definition "the *Illicium anisatum*, a native of China and Japan, the aromatic and carminative fruit of which is used in the preparation of liqueurs. The star-shaped capsules and seeds abound in an essential oil, easily procured by distillation with water. See **ANISEED**. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 371]"@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "doc_star_anise" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Star Anise"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Document-attested minor 19th-century commodity absent as a standalone line in Layer-1 British/Canadian customs ledgers; typically subsumed under htc:0408 (Spices Unenumerated). Attested in: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 371."@en ;
    <ontology/attestationBasis/#resource> "document_attested" ;
    <ontology/dictionarySource/#resource> <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n371> ;
